# 2011 Honda CRF450R – Year-by-Year Fitment Mapping

---

## Identification
- **Brand**: Honda  
- **Model**: CRF450R  
- **Year**: 2011  
- **Generation/Platform Notes**: Continuation of the third-generation platform (2009–2012). The 2011 model received a new suspension linkage ratio and revalved suspension settings for improved cornering stability and rear-end traction. ECU mapping was also slightly revised to aid throttle response.

---

## Sprocket Fitment (Stock)
- **Front Sprocket**: 13T, 520 pitch  
- **Rear Sprocket**: 48T, 520 pitch  
- **Chain Pitch**: 520  
- **Chain Length (Stock)**: 116 links  
- **Front Sprocket Mount Style**: Spline with locking washer  
- **Rear Bolt Pattern / Mount Type**: 6-bolt pattern, standard Honda fitment

---

## Aftermarket Popular Setups
- **Popular Front Sprockets (Racer Spec)**: 13T (standard), 14T (for higher-speed tracks)  
- **Popular Rear Sprockets (Racer Spec)**: 49T, 50T, 51T  
- **Popular Gearing Combos**: 13/49, 13/50, 14/49  
- **Tuning Notes / Reason for Change**: Many riders increased rear sprocket size for quicker acceleration out of corners. Some opted for 14T front for smoother power delivery at higher speeds.

---

